rcepts with the $x$-axis are $(-2,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399414 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399415 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399416 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399417 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399418 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399415 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1080 #uuid "d82b2d36-5f6d-5949-984e-5d1d9ec7556d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399414 1081 "$(0,0,0)$ and $(2,0,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399414 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399414 1084 #uuid "adcb33db-de68-50f5-9cbe-6b7d8f84aaae" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399415 1081 "$(-2,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399415 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399415 1084 #uuid "ee548906-3638-5d51-96d2-b358b4a1f8b6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399416 1081 "$(-4,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399416 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399416 1084 #uuid "81a50ee6-a29f-5cf2-ba44-251758623d8b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1081 "$(4,0,0)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1084 #uuid "ef09c53b-97f7-594e-a8f7-fee68af6a063" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1081 "$(-3\\sqrt{2},0,0)$ and $(3\\sqrt{2},0,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1084 #uuid "b4640bb5-2749-5d8c-bb08-ee4349a6f316" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399420 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1069 "q-73210" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1071 "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=t{e}^{-2t}$, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1072 #uuid "08503449-abde-5746-b6d7-46180193efed" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1074 "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{-2t}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}(1-2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ {e}^{-2t}(1-2t) & >0 \\\\ 1-2t & >0 \\\\ 2t & <1 \\\\ t & <\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is $t\\in [0,\\frac{1}{2}).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399420 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399421 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399420 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399422 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399420 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399423 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399420 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399424 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399420 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399425 13194139533