2 #uuid "a831b1fe-cda9-5ab9-bf01-7acc19edee37" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399439 1074 "The stationary points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.\n\nIn the given graph, we can see that at any point between $x=3$ and $x=4$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at those points.\n\n![](images/ab/ab200bebf80bbd1abe6e0c43ec124fe359da25f38d4346d25d8741decc88aa26.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinates of the stationary points of $f(x)$, are all values in the open interval $(3,4).$ \n\n**Note:** At $x=3$ and $x=4$, there are sharp corners, so ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist at those points. This gives us two more critical points. But they are not stationary points." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399441 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399442 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399443 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399444 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399445 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399443 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1080 #uuid "8aaf3855-a51d-5ca4-8c0a-99b3bc89ed52" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399441 1081 "$x=3$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399441 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399441 1084 #uuid "cb4d5bbd-8b8e-5b87-b552-49eb950fa340" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399442 1081 "$x=3$, $x=4$, and $x=6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399442 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399442 1084 #uuid "25a9ad5d-e3da-5b19-ae3c-1a4da3e2def8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399443 1081 "All points in the open interval $(3,4)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399443 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399443 1084 #uuid "4424aa1e-fbe6-5341-b6bf-db50547251d1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399444 1081 "$x=4$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399444 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399444 1084 #uuid "d8f5049a-410b-5e0f-aa9d-73bdc98cfb29" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399445 1081 "$x=3$ and $x=4$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399445 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399445 1084 #uuid "ae9b2849-1a87-535e-a5be-0fdab3635438" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399446 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399447 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399446 1069 "q-73552" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399446 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399446 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $(x-1)^{2}+4{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\nII. It is a type II region\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399446 1072 #uuid "964e90c7-3ddc-59ef-9c19-6cc6da31e561" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399446 1074 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/21/215dd0c920e700a75896fc54751ec20d197487a2c992cd8910810c66129c14dc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/7e/7e1a0c5dd2b4aadf7efe78d903234b8d00cf4fa92eb7a3b41209a856f2d14b01.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/a9/a90d7306e3f88a31609e368f9362248d6a12b7922b6a9e8c9f980ab31e7fb140.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399448 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399449 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399450 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399451 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399452 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399451 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399447 1080 #uuid "c8f0581f-5142-59ed-84df-f95cc7adf20e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399448 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399448 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399448 1084 #uuid "58331f85-b5fc-59a5-a2ca-f0a6fd38ca0b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399449 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399449 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399449 1084 #uuid "76022809-5efc-5b86-8507-f2ad2e7674e0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1084 #uuid "b0765542-63c4-5076-85eb-d92c5b5ac592" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399451 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399451 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399451 1084 #uuid "20d4565f-595d-51c6-857d-208b49c021b7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1084 #uuid "57eafbb0-6829-567e-b846-7bde9a6cae27" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399454 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1069 "q-73580" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1072 #uuid "09ed8746-0452-52a7-a619-929b2d587f13" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1074 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399455 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399456 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399457 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399458 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399459 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399458 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1080 #uuid "45e63128-e41c-54ad-afda-6808e4f902e4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1084 #uuid "1bbb2c9b-2424-5248-830c-2c1f0a65a08a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1084 #uuid "090537bb-6f40-5836-9945-a970355e758b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1084 #uuid "fab64420-cace-555b-aa98-7c62e22daa9b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399458 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2